y use collateral and  margin calls for example let's say that  you wanted to buy 200 worth of apple  shares but you only have 100  chase will happily loan you the other  100  if you put up your 100 worth of apple  shares as collateral this way they have  quite a bit of leeway apple stock would  have to crash fifty percent for the  total position to be worth less than one  hundred dollars and the second that  apple does reach negative fifty percent  chase will sell all your stock and get  their money back on the other hand if  this stock skyrockets they're happy to  just collect interest and go on with  their day but what if you use the same  100 as collateral with many different  lenders  now as a retail investor banks will make  sure that you don't do this as they  don't really trust you but with someone  like bill they were much looser with  their restrictions which allowed bill to  take on 3-1 5-1 and even 8-1 leverage  bill used this strategy to 100x's  portfolio from 200 million dollars to 20  billion dollars and no one noticed a  thing you see as long as your positions  are playing out there's no problem with  the leverage it's only when your  positions go south that you get wiped  out by 2021 it bill's personal net worth  stood at 20 billion dollars but he was  trading with 100 billion dollars meaning  that he had 80 billion worth of debt  spread across multiple banks this means  that if bill's position dipped to just  20 percent he would have a negative net  worth and he should be margin called but  the banks didn't know this they thought  that they had 40 or 50 worth of leeway  and this became painfully evident when  one of bill's biggest positions crumbled  in march of 2021 vietcom cbs announced  that they would do a share offering  which cost the stock to tumble over 50  percent within a week given that this  was one of arkaigo's biggest positions  banks started a margin called bill and  this is when they realized that they  were screwed not only had bill blown  away his entire net worth but he had  also caused the banks including morgan  stanley goldman sachs credit suisse and  the nomura to incur 10 billion worth of  losses and with that archaicos filed for  bankruptcy  at the end of the day no one really  cared about the banks losing money as it  was due to their own lack of due  diligence but many were sad that bill  lost all his money you would see it  while bill was definitely a degenerate  gambler he was putting his winnings to  good use he wasn't blowing it on yachts  and jets instead he lived an extremely  modest life and donated a total of 590  million dollars to churches schools and  charities and the bill has repeatedly  iterated that his greatest love in life  is god and that the primary reason that  he was chasing money was so that he can  donate it so it's really quite a shame  that things have come to this  but he should have thought about that  before he gambled with 100 billion  dollars but that's just what i think do  you guys think bill has had a net  positive or net negative impact on the  world comment that down below  also drop a like if you respect bill's  balls of steel  and of course consider checking out our  international channels to watch our  videos in different languages and  consider subscribing to see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you

